### ASON bridge — one file to try every HTTP route
###
### Start an application side first:
###     dotnet run --project samples/ConsoleBridgeAppSample              # gRPC :5222, MCP + HTTP :5223
### or  dotnet run --project samples/WpfAppOnlyDemo
###
### Then send the requests below one by one (VS Code REST Client, Rider, or `curl`). @key is empty because the
### development setup has no authorization; fill it in (and start the application with a key) to exercise group 4.

@base = http://localhost:5223
@key =
@contentType = application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Discovery — what does this application expose?
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### The whole contract: protocol version, execution location, capabilities, the operator API, the live instances
GET {{base}}/ason/manifest
Accept: {{contentType}}

### Only the live instances, with the handle that addresses each one
GET {{base}}/ason/instances
Accept: {{contentType}}

### The generated OpenAPI document (the same manifest, rendered for generic HTTP clients and Swagger UI)
GET {{base}}/ason/openapi.json
Accept: {{contentType}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Execution — the two independent interfaces
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Whole script, proxy layer prepended by the application (the default)
POST {{base}}/ason/script
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "return LibDemoStaticOperator.Add(40, 2);" }

### Whole script, sent exactly as it is: the application adds nothing, so the caller owes the proxy layer.
### This one answers 400 execution-failed - only the caller's own code arrived, and `LibDemoStaticOperator` is not
### declared anywhere. It is the honest demonstration of what includeProxyPreamble=false means.
POST {{base}}/ason/script
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "return LibDemoStaticOperator.Add(40, 2);", "includeProxyPreamble": false }

### Body-only mode: the application supplies its proxy layer *and* today's instance declarations, which is how a
### caller whose manifest snapshot went stale is rescued.
POST {{base}}/ason/script
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "return employeesOperator.GetEmployees().Count;", "includeProxyPreamble": false, "includeInstanceDeclarations": true }

### One function, a static module: no handle needed
POST {{base}}/ason/functions/invoke
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "operator": "LibDemoStaticOperator", "method": "Add", "arguments": [20, 22] }

### One function, an instance operator: the handle comes from /ason/instances
POST {{base}}/ason/functions/invoke
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "operator": "EmployeesOperator", "method": "GetEmployees", "handle": "EmployeesOperator" }

### The same call as a path, so it shows up in Swagger UI (the handle may also travel as a query parameter)
POST {{base}}/ason/functions/LibDemoStaticOperator/Add?handle=
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "arguments": [20, 22] }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. The error surface — a refusal is a code, not a paragraph
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### An operator the manifest does not list: 400 + operator-not-found
POST {{base}}/ason/functions/invoke
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "operator": "NoSuchOperator", "method": "Add", "arguments": [1, 2] }

### An instance operator with several live instances and no handle: 400 + handle-ambiguous
### (attach two EmployeesOperator instances first; with one instance the call resolves on its own. On the console
### application side the LibDemo operators are marker-only, so this one answers operator-not-found instead.)
POST {{base}}/ason/functions/invoke
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "operator": "EmployeesOperator", "method": "GetEmployees" }

### A capability that is switched off is not served at all: 404 + not-supported
### (start the application with executeScript disabled to see it)
POST {{base}}/ason/script
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "return 1;" }

### A malformed body is rejected before anything runs: 400 + invalid-arguments
POST {{base}}/ason/script
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Authorization — only meaningful when the application was started with a key
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Without the key: 401 (never 404, which would mean "capability disabled")
GET {{base}}/ason/manifest
Accept: {{contentType}}

### With the key: 200. X-Ason-Bridge-Key is AsonOpenApiBridgeOptions.ApiKeyHeader.
GET {{base}}/ason/manifest
Accept: {{contentType}}
X-Ason-Bridge-Key: {{key}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Streaming — server-sent events, one request per line: `event: log`* then `event: result|error`
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Watch a script run (the REST Client shows the stream as it arrives; with curl add -N to disable buffering)
POST {{base}}/ason/script/stream
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "code": "return LibDemoStaticOperator.Add(40, 2);" }
